  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "#Device Three\r\n\r\n###Denise Carter — Farmer\r\n\r\nDenise flies a camera drone over her sweet potato and soybean fields to spot trouble early. The drone runs on a battery and transfers its images to her laptop over Wi-Fi once it lands. Images are kept on the laptop's drive and backed up to the cloud\r\n\r\n* The laptop freezes when she opens a whole field's images at once.\r\n* It now says there isn't enough space to save this week's flight.\r\n* Transferring one flight takes the entire evening.\r\n* The drone stays up about 18 minutes, not the 25 printed on the box.",
    "hide_share_and_remix": "false",
    "require_edit_to_continue": "true",
